{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Shall the prey be taken, etc.</b> The words of the prophet speak on Israel's behalf, for they were saying: How shall Israel go forth from the hand of the nations?" "<b>Shall the prey be taken from the mighty one.</b> The taken one that was taken, and it is the captivity." "<b>Or the captive of the righteous delivered.</b> On account of his righteousness, after the mighty one took him."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:50.192041551Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}